// The write path, and the one rule that governs it.
//
// Paste into https://app.eraser.io as a Sequence diagram.
//
// NOTHING after the ack boundary can lose data. NOTHING before it may perform
// analytics, touch ClickHouse, classify payloads, or run any operation whose
// latency we do not control. Every step below is placed relative to that line,
// which is the only reason the order matters.

title Write Path — the ack boundary is the whole design

MCP Server [icon: python]
Ingest Gateway [icon: lock]
Postgres [icon: postgresql]
Redis [icon: redis]
Collector [icon: layers]
Kafka [icon: kafka]

MCP Server > Ingest Gateway: POST /v1/traces (OTLP protobuf)
activate Ingest Gateway

Ingest Gateway > Postgres: resolve API key or verify session JWT
Postgres > Ingest Gateway: tenant · project · plan · quotas

opt [label: "session JWT — verified LOCALLY, no lookup"] {
  Ingest Gateway > Ingest Gateway: "check aud · kid · exp · epoch\ningest must not depend on Redis being up"
}

Ingest Gateway > Redis: quota check
alt [label: "hard quota exceeded"] {
  Redis > Ingest Gateway: over limit
  Ingest Gateway > MCP Server: 429 — rejected before Kafka
}
else [label: "soft quota exceeded"] {
  Ingest Gateway > Ingest Gateway: "stamp mcpobs.quota.soft_exceeded\na warning only we can see is not a warning"
}
else [label: "within quota"] {
  Redis > Ingest Gateway: ok
}

Ingest Gateway > Ingest Gateway: "validate OTLP structure"
Ingest Gateway > Ingest Gateway: "OVERWRITE tenant/project/region from the\nauthenticated key — inbound resource attributes\nare an assertion by an untrusted party"

Ingest Gateway > Collector: forward OTLP, tenant stamped
deactivate Ingest Gateway
activate Collector
Collector > Collector: memory_limiter → batch (1s / 512 spans)
Collector > Kafka: produce · key=tenant_id · acks=all · zstd
activate Kafka
Kafka > Collector: durably accepted
deactivate Kafka
Collector > Ingest Gateway: 200
deactivate Collector
Ingest Gateway > MCP Server: "200 ◄════ ACK BOUNDARY ════\nreturned ONLY past this line"
